{"id": "SGU_Episode_669", "title": "SGU Episode 669", "type": "structured", "description": "The Skeptic's Guide to the Universe, Episode 669 Transcript", "metadata": {"title": "SGU Episode 669", "date": "May 5 2024", "year": 2024, "month": 5, "day": 5, "rogues": ["Steven Novella", "Jay Novella", "Evan Bernstein", "Bob Novella", "Cara Santa Maria"], "quotee_url": "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frank_Zappa", "quote": "\n Reality is what it is, not what you want it to be. \n", "quotee": "\n Frank Zappa ", "quotee_title": " American musician\n", "guests": [{"guest": "Ethan Winer", "guest_title": " recording engineer", "guest_url": "https://ethanwiner.com"}], "categories": [], "podcast_url": "https://www.theskepticsguide.org/podcasts/episode-669", "episode_number": 669}, "sections": [{"id": 0, "text": "Voice-over: You're listening to the Skeptics' Guide to the Universe, your escape to reality.\n", "title": "Introduction, SGU Anniversary, announcements", "metadata": {"title": "Introduction, SGU Anniversary, announcements"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 1, "text": "Fallacy[v 1]\n_text_with_mention_of_vagiliy_wtw_episode_\n", "title": "What's the Word?", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:08:20", "hour": 0, "minute": "8", "second": "20", "title": "What's the Word?"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 2, "text": "", "title": "News Items", "metadata": {"title": "News Items"}, "sections": [{"id": 3, "text": "", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}, {"id": 4, "text": "", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "B", "speaker": "Bob Novella"}}, {"id": 5, "text": "", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "C", "speaker": "Cara Santa Maria"}}, {"id": 6, "text": "", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "J", "speaker": "Jay Novella"}}, {"id": 7, "text": "", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "E", "speaker": "Evan Bernstein"}}, {"id": 8, "text": "(laughs)\n(laughter)\n(applause)\n[inaudible]", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "E", "speaker": "Evan Bernstein"}}, {"id": 9, "text": "\nEarth's magnetic field may not be flipping\u00a0[2]\n\n\n", "title": "Flipping Magnetic Fields", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:13:37", "hour": 0, "minute": "13", "second": "37", "links": ["https://arstechnica.com/science/2018/05/earths-magnetic-field-may-not-be-flipping/"], "title": "Flipping Magnetic Fields"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 10, "text": "\nNASA greenlights self-assembling space telescope\u00a0[3]\n\n\n", "title": "Self-Assembling Space Telescope", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:21:56", "hour": 0, "minute": "21", "second": "56", "links": ["https://phys.org/news/2018-05-nasa-greenlights-self-assembling-space-telescope.html"], "title": "Self-Assembling Space Telescope"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 11, "text": "\nGunshot-wound dynamics model for John F. Kennedy assassination\u00a0[4]\n\n\n", "title": "JFK Headshot", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:28:58", "hour": 0, "minute": "28", "second": "58", "links": ["https://www.cell.com/heliyon/fulltext/S2405-8440(17)33188-2"], "title": "JFK Headshot"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 12, "text": "\nWhat's Wrong With Growing Blobs of Brain Tissue?\u00a0[1]\u00a0\n\n\n", "title": "Growing Brains", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:41:30", "hour": 0, "minute": "41", "second": "30", "links": ["https://www.theatlantic.com/science/archive/2018/04/what-happens-as-we-get-better-at-artificially-growing-brains/558881/?utm_source=feed"], "title": "Growing Brains"}, "sections": []}]}, {"id": 13, "text": "", "title": "Who's That Noisy?", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:52:20", "hour": 0, "minute": "52", "second": "20", "title": "Who's That Noisy?"}, "sections": [{"id": 14, "text": "[Horn-like squeaking, increasing in frequency]\n\nshort_text_from_transcript\n", "title": "New Noisy", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:54:33", "hour": 0, "minute": "54", "second": "33", "title": "New Noisy"}, "sections": []}]}, {"id": 15, "text": "", "title": "Questions/Emails/Corrections/Follow-ups", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:54:57", "hour": 0, "minute": "54", "second": "57", "title": "Questions/Emails/Corrections/Follow-ups"}, "sections": [{"id": 16, "text": "", "title": "Correction #1: Annealing WTW", "metadata": {"title": "Correction #1: Annealing WTW"}, "sections": []}]}, {"id": 17, "text": "Ethan Winer, recording engineer", "title": "Interview with Ethan Winer", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:59:51", "hour": 0, "minute": "59", "second": "51", "links": ["https://ethanwiner.com/book.htm"], "title": "Interview with Ethan Winer"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 18, "text": "Voice-over: It's time for Science or Fiction.\n", "title": "Science or Fiction", "metadata": {"timestamp": "1:21:41", "hour": "1", "minute": "21", "second": "41", "title": "Science or Fiction"}, "sections": [{"id": 19, "text": "", "title": "Evan's Response", "metadata": {"title": "Evan's Response"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 20, "text": "", "title": "Cara's Response", "metadata": {"title": "Cara's Response"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 21, "text": "", "title": "Bob's Response", "metadata": {"title": "Bob's Response"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 22, "text": "", "title": "Jay's Response", "metadata": {"title": "Jay's Response"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 23, "text": "", "title": "Steve Explains Item #4", "metadata": {"title": "Steve Explains Item #4"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 24, "text": "", "title": "Steve Explains Item #3", "metadata": {"title": "Steve Explains Item #3"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 25, "text": "", "title": "Steve Explains Item #2", "metadata": {"title": "Steve Explains Item #2"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 26, "text": "", "title": "Steve Explains Item #1", "metadata": {"title": "Steve Explains Item #1"}, "sections": []}]}, {"id": 27, "text": "", "title": "Skeptical Quote of the Week", "metadata": {"timestamp": "1:40:41", "hour": "1", "minute": "40", "second": "41", "title": "Skeptical Quote of the Week"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 28, "text": "", "title": "Signoff/Announcements", "metadata": {"timestamp": "1:41:57", "hour": "1", "minute": "41", "second": "57", "title": "Signoff/Announcements"}, "sections": [{"id": 29, "text": "\u2014and until next week, this is your  Skeptics' Guide to the Universe.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}, {"id": 30, "text": "Skeptics' Guide to the Universe is produced by SGU Productions, dedicated to promoting science and critical thinking. For more information, visit us at theskepticsguide.org. Send your questions to info@theskepticsguide.org. And, if you would like to support the show and all the work that we do, go to patreon.com/SkepticsGuide and consider becoming a patron and becoming part of the SGU community. Our listeners and supporters are what make SGU possible.", "metadata": {"links": ["http://www.theskepticsguide.org", "https://www.patreon.com/SkepticsGuide"], "speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}]}, {"id": 31, "text": "", "title": "Today I Learned", "metadata": {"title": "Today I Learned"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 32, "text": "\n\u2191 1.0 1.1 The Atlantic: What's Wrong With Growing Blobs of Brain Tissue?\n\n\u2191 Ars Technica: Earth's magnetic field may not be flipping\n\n\u2191 Cornell University: NASA greenlights self-assembling space telescope\n\n\u2191 Heliyon: Gunshot-wound dynamics model for John F. Kennedy assassination\n\n\u2191 NWF Blog:\u00a012 Things to Know about Mistletoe (updated 12/2022)\n\n\u2191 Current Biology:\u00a0Absence of Complex I Is Associated with Diminished Respiratory Chain Function in European Mistletoe\n\n\u2191 Online Etymology Dictionary:\u00a0mistletoe (n.)\n\n\u2191 NWF Blog:\u00a012 Things to Know about Mistletoe (updated 12/2012)\n\n\u2191 [url_for_TIL publication: title]\n\n", "title": "References", "metadata": {"links": ["https://www.theatlantic.com/science/archive/2018/04/what-happens-as-we-get-better-at-artificially-growing-brains/558881/", "https://arstechnica.com/science/2018/05/earths-magnetic-field-may-not-be-flipping/", "https://phys.org/news/2018-05-nasa-greenlights-self-assem